@startuml
!include _style.puml
title Product State and Stock Updates
hide empty description
[*] --> ACTIVE : normal createProduct()\n[stock >= 0; default status]
ACTIVE --> OUT_OF_STOCK : updateProduct(stock=0 or status=OUT_OF_STOCK)\nor validateAndDeductStock() [remaining=0]
OUT_OF_STOCK --> ACTIVE : updateProduct(stock > 0 or status=ACTIVE)\nor ProductService.restoreStock() [newStock > 0]
ACTIVE --> INACTIVE : updateProduct(status=INACTIVE)
OUT_OF_STOCK --> INACTIVE : updateProduct(status=INACTIVE)
INACTIVE --> ACTIVE : updateProduct(status=ACTIVE)
INACTIVE --> OUT_OF_STOCK : updateProduct(status=OUT_OF_STOCK)
ACTIVE --> ACTIVE : InventoryService.reserve/release()\nor SubOrderService.restoreStock() / change stock only
OUT_OF_STOCK --> OUT_OF_STOCK : InventoryService.release()\nor SubOrderService.restoreStock() / change stock only
INACTIVE --> INACTIVE : stock update / remain INACTIVE\nunless explicit status supplied

note right of ACTIVE
createProduct allows stock=0 but defaults status to ACTIVE.
Checkout InventoryService.reserve requires ACTIVE product/shop
and sufficient stock, but does not set OUT_OF_STOCK at zero.
Catalog availability also requires stock > 0, active shop and active seller User.
An explicit updateProduct status overrides automatic stock logic;
any enum value is accepted, including the current value.
end note
note left of OUT_OF_STOCK
ProductService restoreStock reactivates OUT_OF_STOCK.
InventoryService release and SubOrderService restoreStock
only increase stock, without reactivating product status.
INACTIVE stock changes do not automatically activate a product.
These paths are intentionally shown as implemented.
end note
